"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-k7.1--plan/meta.json","size_bytes":6224},"prompt":{"digest":"8581a69f0c1a7b75b22c3588b8097a4e465d53c7d055c879bb69aa04482a9570","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-k7.1--plan/prompt.md","size_bytes":184},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"9786094954a05a5b04ef5beb5cadf57a58cf27f08d0565369b2b49e2241e2636","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-k7.1--plan/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":7906},"state":{"digest":"363a31261f803fe6625b34e4fd9775ec17d7cb6a9438b4e5f2b5fee70480fb85","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-k7.1--plan/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-11-11T13:24:26.195517+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-k7.1--plan","local_name":"bob-cli-k7.1--plan","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-k7","agent_clan_generation":"20261111075939","agent_session":"bob-cli-k7.1","agent_session_role":"plan","bead_id":"bob-cli-k7.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-k7[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Keep-moving marks — show `⏭ N` after a Task Link whose close will [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]keep its project moving[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]In today's ledger, a quiet `⏭ N` mark after a Task Link forecasts [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the `Keep ‹N› moving` successor picker that closing that task will [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]really open: N is exactly the number of rows that group will offer,[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]it appears only on the link whose close triggers the group, and it [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]is silent whenever that cannot be proven. Keep-moving first stops [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]skipping standalone top-level projects (only umbrella projects are [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]skipped), so the screenshot's `job_email_recruiters` link shows `⏭ [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]4` and Ctrl+Enter then offers those same four tasks.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]keep_moving_link_marks.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/keep_moving_link_marks.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-k7[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-k7/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Umbrella rule in the contract, memory, and Rust[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]umbrella-rule[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]umbrella-rule: in bob-cli, redefine leaf projects as every recognised [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project except umbrellas (root projects whose ^prj carries a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Sub-projects line); update §12.15–§12.17, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]projects/pomodoro-homes/json-outputs docs, the accepted memory [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]decisions, and Rust is_leaf_project plus its LP/KM tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Umbrella rule and `_generated/` fix in the Obsidian cycler[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]umbrella-cycler[dim] · [dim][/dim]after umbrella-rule[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]umbrella-cycler: in the bob-plugins task-status-cycler, apply the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]umbrella rule in successorLeafProject using the planner's held note [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]text, stop generated tag pages from making parent stems ambiguous, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]update LP/KM tests and docs, build, and sync.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Keep-moving mark display contract[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]mark-contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]after umbrella-rule[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mark-contract: in bob-cli docs, add docs/keep-moving-marks.md (the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]authoritative display contract with the KB/KT/KP vectors from this [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plan), register it, cross-link it from frees-marks and §12.15, and move [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the off-clock chip contract to side 4.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Pure keep-moving mark core and cross-plugin parity[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mark-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]after umbrella-cycler, mark-contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mark-core: in bob-ledger-tools, add the pure, synchronous gates, leaf [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]predicate, offer count, tooltip, DOM builder, and widget class, plus [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]config readers, the vector tests, and an identity-set parity test [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]against the cycler's real successor planner.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Live Preview, Reading view, look, and liveness[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mark-surface[dim] · [dim][/dim]after mark-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mark-surface: in bob-ledger-tools, render the mark in Live Preview and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Reading view, with the shared source-text cache, refresh triggers, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]baton-pass tick, toggle, CSS, off-clock chip at side 4, docs, a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]real-Obsidian e2e, build, and sync.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Real-vault audit against capture and the picker[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]audit[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ma